                <pb facs="0640" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Standard Oil/375: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kornfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-30T11:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                                1924—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Sinclair representative here has been asked by Persian Government to give
                    written engagement to defend rights under concession as against any claims based
                    on grant by Imperial firman to Sepahsalar which was afterwards transferred to
                    Khoshtaria, and to waive claim of any sort upon the Persian Government should an
                    adverse judgment disallow Sinclair’s title.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kornfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
